From: vmapp <vmapp@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] ui: "No thanks, I'll use Ollama locally" goes to the chat, not to the "Run Ollama" screen

First run: Welcome > "Create an account" > "No thanks, I'll use Ollama locally" saves the onboarding as done and shows a last screen, "Run Ollama",
with a command to copy into a terminal. In the desktop app that screen is not a dead end because the tray icon stays: the user opens the
chat from it. A window without a tray (a vmapp window) has nothing to go on with: no button, no link, no navigation, until the app is
started again. This sends the user to the chat (route "/") as soon as the choice is saved, which is where the tray would have taken them.
The other way out of onboarding (signing in) is unchanged, and so is the rest of the first-run flow.

---
 app/ui/app/src/components/Onboarding.tsx | 3 +--
 app/ui/app/src/routes/onboarding.tsx     | 7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/ui/app/src/components/Onboarding.tsx b/app/ui/app/src/components/Onboarding.tsx
--- a/app/ui/app/src/components/Onboarding.tsx
+++ b/app/ui/app/src/components/Onboarding.tsx
@@ -1274,8 +1274,7 @@ export default function Onboarding(props: OnboardingProps) {
       onRetryCompletion={() => void leave()}
       onLocal={() => {
         if (leavingRef.current) return;
-        props.onUseLocal();
-        setStep("run");
+        props.onUseLocal(); // saves the choice and goes to the chat; no "Run Ollama" step
       }}
     />
   );
diff --git a/app/ui/app/src/routes/onboarding.tsx b/app/ui/app/src/routes/onboarding.tsx
--- a/app/ui/app/src/routes/onboarding.tsx
+++ b/app/ui/app/src/routes/onboarding.tsx
@@ -88,8 +88,11 @@ function OnboardingRoute() {
   }, [setSettings, settingsData]);

   const finishSetup = useCallback(() => {
-    void completeOnboarding();
-  }, [completeOnboarding]);
+    // The desktop app stays on the "Run Ollama" screen here and the user goes on from the tray. A window without a tray goes to the chat.
+    void completeOnboarding().then((done) => {
+      if (done) void navigate({ to: "/" });
+    });
+  }, [completeOnboarding, navigate]);

   const openApps = useCallback(async (): Promise<boolean> => {
     if (!(await completeOnboarding())) return false;
